.git
# Note the `**/` on each of these. Docker anchors a pattern at the context root
# unless it starts with `**/`, so a bare `__pycache__/` or `.venv/` matches only a
# root-level one — and this repo has neither at the root (they live under
# app/server-python/). Without the prefix all three lines silently matched nothing:
# the 67MB venv was shipped to the daemon on every build, and src/__pycache__ +
# src/<app>/__pycache__ were copied into the image, carrying stale bytecode for
# modules that no longer exist. Verified by building a probe image that COPYs the
# whole context and lists it.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
# desktop/README.md is deliberately NOT ignored. desktop/pyproject.toml declares
# `readme = "README.md"`, and uv reads it when generating the desktop package's
# metadata during the dependency resolve — so excluding it fails the build. The
# same holds for desktop/pyproject.toml itself, and for the workspace root's
# pyproject.toml and uv.lock.
# The web client's source IS in the build context (the web-build stage needs it),
# but its install/build artifacts must not be — they'd bloat the context and the
# image rebuilds them from the lockfile anyway.
app/client-web/node_modules/
app/client-web/dist/
# Generated by the web-build stage inside the image; never ship a local copy.
app/server-python/src/static/

# --- Desktop package exclusions (desktop/, the p-swamp package) --------------
#
# The build context is the repo root, and the runtime stage installs the desktop
# package from desktop/src/ as an editable path dependency (see the Dockerfile).
# It needs the manifest, README and src/ and nothing else, so everything below
# is kept out of the daemon upload entirely.
#
# build/ is the big one: local build artifacts, currently ~1.6 GB. examples/ is
# ~13 MB of simulation cases, and the sample dataset the server replays is
# already committed under app/server-python/src/pswamp_web/data/. The root-level
# build/, examples/ and tests/ are kept too, in case an old checkout still has
# untracked leftovers there from before the desktop package moved.
desktop/build/
desktop/examples/
desktop/tests/
build/
examples/
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.idea/
# The core's tests (the rules above are anchored to their directories), and
# each module's own tests/ folder beside its code.
core/tests/
modules/**/tests/
